## Exploration Report: TypeScript Component Architecture & Animation Patterns

### 1. **Animation Class Pattern**

**Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/animation/Animation.ts` (base class)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/animation/TextReveal.ts` (static-based animation)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/animation/BlockReveal.ts` (state-driven animation)

**Key Pattern:**
- **Base Class:** `Animation` is an abstract base providing `resolveElements()` static method
- **TextReveal:** Uses static methods exclusively; state managed via DOM dataset attributes (`data-reveal`, `data-mask`)
- **BlockReveal:** Uses static methods with class-based state management (applies CSS classes like `is-block-reveal-up`)
- Both use `ObserveManager` for Intersection Observer patterns
- Both have `init()`, `dispose()`, `prepare()`, `observe()`, `reveal/riseUp()` static methods

---

### 2. **UI Component Pattern**

**Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/ui/UI.ts` (base class)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/ui/Drawer.ts` (instance-based with lifecycle)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/ui/ContactWizard.ts` (complex instance-based component)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/ui/WorkCard.ts` (Three.js canvas-based utility)

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// Base class hierarchy
UI (abstract)
  ├─ Drawer (extends UI)
  ├─ HudPanel (extends UI)
  └─ NormalOverlay (extends UI)

// Static registry pattern
UI.getOrCreate<T>(Subclass, config): T
  // Singleton pattern with config storage
```

- **Lifecycle:** `init()` → `mount()` → `dispose()`
- **Config Pattern:** All options extend `ComponentConfig` (from `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/dom.types.js`)
- **Element Binding:** Via `selector` in config; found at init time with `document.querySelector()`
- **Visibility Management:** `setVisibleOn()` / `setVisibleOff()` → `_setVisibility()` → `applyVisibility()`
- **Static Factory Pattern:** `getInstance(options)` creates or reuses singleton

---

### 3. **Generic Component Pattern**

**Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/components/Component.ts` (base class)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/components/CustomCursor.ts` (instance-based)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/components/Toast.ts` (stateless factory)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/components/Marquee.ts` (static utility)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/components/Button.ts` (partial view - 100 lines)

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// Component.ts interface
abstract class Component implements IUIComponent {
  protected _disposed = false;
  init(): void
  protected abstract mount(): void
  protected abstract applyVisibility(visible: boolean): void
  abstract getVisibleState(): boolean
  setVisibleOn/Off(): void
}
```

- **CustomCursor:** Static singleton (`CustomCursor.instance`), manages custom cursor DOM element
- **Toast:** Static viewport + factory pattern, creates per-message toast elements
- **Marquee:** Fully static, manages array of `MarqueeItemRuntime` instances internally
- All have `static init()` and `static dispose()` entry points

---

### 4. **GSAP Integration Pattern**

**Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/gsap.types.ts` (type definitions)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/global.d.ts` (window extensions)

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// GSAP is accessed via window global, NOT imported as module
function getGsap(): GsapGlobal | undefined {
  return (window as WindowWithGsap).gsap;
}

// Window extension (global.d.ts)
declare global {
  interface Window {
    gsap?: import("gsap").gsap;
    ScrollTrigger?: typeof import("gsap/ScrollTrigger").ScrollTrigger;
  }
}

// Type interfaces for GSAP objects
interface GsapGlobal {
  timeline: (vars?: object) => GSAPTimeline;
  to(target: unknown, vars: object): unknown;
  killTweensOf?(target: unknown): void;
  set(target: unknown, vars: object): void;
  fromTo(...): unknown;
}

interface GSAPTimeline extends TimelineControlMethods {
  to(target: unknown, vars: object, position?: TimelinePosition): this;
  from(...): this;
  // ... more methods
}
```

**Usage Examples:**
- **Drawer:** Stores active tweens in WeakMap, gets GSAP via helper, calls `gsap.killTweensOf()`
- **Marquee:** Uses `gsap.to()` for infinite repeating animation, includes fallback CSS animation
- Both check `if (!gsap)` before usage (GSAP may not be loaded)

---

### 5. **Registration & Initialization Pattern**

**Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/app/UiSetup.ts` (registry example)

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// UI components registered in arrays
const UI_COMPONENT_ENTRIES: readonly UiTimelineComponentEntry[] = [
  { key: drawer, factory: () => Drawer.getInstance({...}) },
  { key: gauge, factory: () => HudPanel.getInstance() },
  { key: normalOverlay, factory: () => NormalOverlay.getInstance() },
];

// Initialization sequence
_mountTimelineTargets(): void {
  for (const { key, factory } of UI_COMPONENT_ENTRIES) {
    const instance = factory();
    instance.init();              // Call init to mount
    resolver.registerTarget(instance);  // Register for timeline
  }
}
```

- Components are **lazily created** via factory functions
- **Singleton pattern** via `getInstance()` 
- **Timeline integration:** Registered with `TimelineRuntime` for animation orchestration
- **Cleanup:** Disposed in reverse with `instance.dispose()` + `resolver.unregisterTarget()`

---

### 6. **Configuration & Constants Pattern**

**Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/config/component.config.ts` (main config)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/component.types.ts` (type definitions)

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// ALL configuration in one config object with named sections
export const TOAST = { durationMs: 1800, enterDelayMs: 24, ... } as const;
export const MARQUEE = { selector, viewportSelector, trackSelector, ... } as const;
export const CONTACT_WIZARD = { selector, transitionMs, ... } as const;

// Corresponding types
export interface ToastNotifier { setVisibleOn(message, variant?): void; }
export interface MarqueeInitOptions { root?: ParentNode; selector?: string; }
export interface ContactWizardInitOptions { root?: ParentNode; }
```

- **No magic numbers** in code; all constants in config files
- Each config object is `as const` for type safety
- Provides defaults; options override via destructuring

---

### 7. **DOM Element Binding Pattern**

**Files:**
- All components use selector-based binding (CSS selectors in data-attributes)

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// Static binding
const elements = TextReveal.resolveElements(selector);
const elements = BlockReveal.resolveElements(selector);

// Instance binding
constructor(config: DrawerConfig = { selector: "..." }) {
  this.config = config;
}
init(): void {
  const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(this.config.selector);
  this.setElement(el);
  this.mount();
}

// Static utility pattern
Marquee.init(options): void {
  const selector = options.selector ?? MARQUEE.selector;
  const root = options.root ?? document;
  root.querySelectorAll(selector).forEach(el => { ... });
}
```

- **No constructor-based DOM queries** (lazy binding at `init()` time)
- **Support for scoping** via optional `root?: ParentNode` parameter
- **Data attributes** for configuration: `data-reveal`, `data-wizard-step`, etc.

---

### 8. **Hover Animation & Event Binding Pattern**

**Example from Drawer:**
```typescript
// Store tweens in WeakMap to avoid memory leaks
private static _activeTweens = new WeakMap<HTMLElement, { open?: GsapTweenLike; close?: GsapTweenLike }>();

// Bind event in mount()
private _mountTrigger(root: HTMLElement): void {
  const trigger = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(this._triggerSelector);
  trigger.addEventListener("click", this._boundFlipVisibility);
}

// Unbind event in dispose()
override dispose(): void {
  if (this._triggerEl) {
    this._triggerEl.removeEventListener("click", this._boundFlipVisibility);
    this._triggerEl = null;
  }
  super.dispose();
}

// GSAP usage for hover
const gsap = getGsap();
if (gsap && typeof gsap.killTweensOf === 'function') {
  gsap.killTweensOf(target);  // Kill existing tweens
}
// Create new tween
gsap.to(target, { duration: 0.3, opacity: 1, ease: "power2.out" });
```

---

### 9. **Type Safety Pattern**

**Key Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/component.types.ts` (all component types)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/gsap.types.ts` (GSAP interface types)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/types/engine.types.ts` (IUIComponent, IVisible, ITimelineActionTarget)

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// No inline types; all in types/ folder
export interface CustomCursorOptions { root?: ParentNode; disableSelector?: string; }
export type CustomCursorState = "idle" | "interactive";
export interface MarqueeItem { elements: MarqueeElements; speed: number; ... }

// Typed window globals
interface WindowWithGsap extends Window {
  gsap?: GsapGlobal;
  ScrollTrigger?: ScrollTriggerGlobal;
}

// Typed DOM config
