### 10. **Three.js Integration Example (WorkCard)**

**File:** `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/ui/WorkCard.ts`

**Key Pattern:**
```typescript
// Static utility class (no instance required)
export class WorkCard {
  static buildTexture(proj, size, image?, options?): THREE.CanvasTexture { ... }
  static updateTextureImage(texture, proj, size, image, options?): void { ... }
  static createMesh(proj, size, detailPath, options?): THREE.Mesh { ... }
  static loadImage(url): Promise<HTMLImageElement> { ... }
}

// Texture caching
private static texCache = new Map<string, THREE.CanvasTexture>();

// Disposal pattern
static offTextures(): void {
  texCache.forEach((texture) => texture.dispose());
  texCache.clear();
}
```

---

## Summary: Pattern for Creating New Self-Contained Component

### **Architecture Pattern:**
1. **Extend Component or UI base class** (not Animation—those are reveal-only)
2. **Static factory method**: `static init(options)` or `getInstance(config)`
3. **Config object in component.config.ts**: With selector and options
4. **Type definitions in component.types.ts**: For all options/interfaces
5. **Lifecycle methods**: `mount()` (init), `dispose()` (cleanup)
6. **Event binding**: Store bound callbacks as instance properties, bind in `mount()`, unbind in `dispose()`
7. **GSAP access**: Via `(window as WindowWithGsap).gsap` with null checks
8. **No global imports**: Use window globals or config constants only

### **File Structure:**
```
resource/ts/
  ├─ components/YourComponent.ts
  ├─ config/component.config.ts (add YOUR_CONFIG export)
  ├─ types/component.types.ts (add YourComponentOptions interface)
  └─ app/UiSetup.ts or ComponentSetup.ts (register via factory)
```

### **GSAP Hover Animation Example Pattern:**
```typescript
private _tween: GsapTweenLike | null = null;

private _onMouseEnter = (): void => {
  const gsap = (window as WindowWithGsap).gsap;
  if (!gsap) return;
  gsap.killTweensOf(this.element);
  this._tween = gsap.to(this.element, {
    duration: 0.3,
    opacity: 1,
    ease: "power2.out",
  }) as GsapTweenLike;
};

private _onMouseLeave = (): void => {
  const gsap = (window as WindowWithGsap).gsap;
  if (!gsap) return;
  gsap.killTweensOf(this.element);
  this._tween = gsap.to(this.element, {
    duration: 0.3,
    opacity: 0.5,
    ease: "power2.out",
  }) as GsapTweenLike;
};

protected mount(): void {
  this.element?.addEventListener("mouseenter", this._onMouseEnter);
  this.element?.addEventListener("mouseleave", this._onMouseLeave);
}

override dispose(): void {
  this.element?.removeEventListener("mouseenter", this._onMouseEnter);
  this.element?.removeEventListener("mouseleave", this._onMouseLeave);
  this._tween?.kill?.();
  super.dispose();
}
```

