### Integration Notes

#### `killTweensOf` optionality

The real `GsapGlobal` in the codebase (line 131 of `gsap.types.ts`) has `killTweensOf?` marked optional. The component uses `gsap.killTweensOf?.(...)` optional-chaining throughout, which is correct. The prompt's stub marks it non-optional — the actual codebase takes precedence.

#### `overwrite` property on GSAP vars

`overwrite: "auto"` is passed inside the `vars` object (`gsap.to(target, vars)`). Since the method signature is `to(target: unknown, vars: object): unknown`, TypeScript accepts any `object` literal here — no type widening issues.

#### `for...of` string iteration for Korean characters

Korean Hangul syllable blocks (e.g. `무`) are single code points and single UTF-16 code units, so `split("")` would also work, but `for...of` is the correct approach for full Unicode correctness (surrogate pairs in emoji) and matches the intent.

#### Stagger on array targets

Passing `this._origChars` (an `HTMLElement[]`) as the first argument to `gsap.to` is valid — GSAP accepts arrays. The `stagger` property inside vars applies the per-element delay.

